  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "special_value",
    "affected_api": "sklearn.impute.KNNImputer",
    "observed_behavior": "With weights='uniform', KNNImputer._calc_impute (sklearn/impute/_knn.py) does not set nan-distance donors to zero weight, so the donor with nan distance is included in the kNN mean and the imputed value is 1.5 instead of 1.",
    "expected_behavior": "Donors with nan distance should be excluded from the mean for uniform weights, as they already are for distance weights, giving 1 for the imputed value.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "weights='uniform'",
      "a training sample whose distance to the query row is nan (for example, the donor has nan in a feature used by nan_euclidean_distances)",
      "n_neighbors=2 with the toy dataset X_train=[[1,1],[nan,2]] and X_test=[[0,nan]]"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "X_train=[[1, 1], [np.nan, 2]]; X_test=[[0, np.nan]]; KNNImputer(n_neighbors=2, weights='uniform').fit(X_train).transform(X_test)",
        "buggy_output": "[[0, 1.5]]",
        "expected_output": "[[0, 1]]",
        "value_kind": "float",
        "source": "issue#29079"
      },
      {
        "input": "Same X_train and X_test with KNNImputer(n_neighbors=2, weights='distance')",
        "buggy_output": "[[0, 1]]",
        "expected_output": "[[0, 1]]",
        "value_kind": "float",
        "source": "issue#29079"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "Issue reports expected results [[0, 1]] for both uniform and distance weights",
      "Added test test_knn_imputer_nan_distance"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "nan_euclidean_distances([[0, nan]], [[1, 1], [nan, 2]]) returns [[1.41421356, nan]], so the second training sample has a NaN distance to the query.",
      "With weights='uniform', KNNImputer(n_neighbors=2) currently includes the NaN-distance donor in the mean, giving imputed value 1.5 instead of expected 1.",
      "With weights='distance', the NaN-distance donor is already excluded (weight set to 0), giving the expected imputed value 1.",
      "Proposed fix in _calc_impute: when weight_matrix is None (uniform weights), set weight_matrix = np.ones_like(donors_dist) and weight_matrix[np.isnan(donors_dist)] = 0.0, so NaN-distance samples are excluded from the mean.",
      "Special value involved is NaN (nan distance), entering via nan_euclidean_distances; correct handling is zero weight for nan-distance donors. No inf or signed-zero or subnormal evidence in passages.",
      "Tests parametrized over na in [-1, np.nan] and weights in ['uniform', 'distance'] were added (test_knn_imputer_nan_distance)."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "The issue's Actual Results and Expected Results are shown without dtype or precision, so dtype, precision and exact comparison tolerance are unspecified in the evidence.",
      "The defect is shown for uniform weights and not distance weights, but no dtype difference is stated in the passages.",
      "A separate discussion notes all-NaN datasets still take about 7 seconds because pairwise distances are computed; this is a performance concern, not a numerical special-value handling requirement.",
      "Magnitude regime is not stated beyond the small toy values (imputed value 1 vs 1.5)."
    ]
  },
